Hello,<br><br>I am trying to compile a single simple concordance for &#39;may&#39; and &#39;may<br>not&#39; as node expressions. &#39;May&#39;s do get retrieved but not the &#39;not&#39;s<br>in &#39;may not&#39; cases.<br><br>Any tips on how to make it work? I have tried a number of possible<br>regular expressions for &#39;may not&#39; but unsuccessfully.<br><br>Below is the script I used, it is based on section 4.2 of Quantitative<br>Corpus Linguistics with R, p.127-135:<br><br><br>DATAFILE&lt;-scan(choose.files(),what=&quot;char&quot;,sep=&quot;
&quot;)<br>DATAFILE2&lt;-unlist(strsplit(DATAFILE,&quot;\W+&quot;))<br>DATAFILE2&lt;-gsub(&quot;(\W)&quot;,&quot;\1&quot;,DATAFILE,perl=T)<br>DATAFILE3&lt;-unlist(strsplit(DATAFILE2,&quot; +&quot;))<br>tail(DATAFILE3)<br><br>(matches.in.datafile&lt;-grep(&quot;(^may$|^may.not<br>$)&quot;,DATAFILE3,ignore.case=T))<br>DATAFILE3[(matches.in.datafile[2]-6):(matches.in.datafile[2]+6)]<br>beginning.of.range&lt;-max(1,(matches.in.datafile[1]-6))<br><br>conc.outputfile&lt;-choose.files()<br>cat(&quot;PRECEDING_CONTEXT	MATCH	SUBSEQUENT_CONTEXT<br>
&quot;,file=conc.outputfile)<br><br> for(i in matches.in.datafile) {<br> cat(file=conc.outputfile,append=T,<br> DATAFILE3[max(0,i-6):max(0,i-1)],<br> &quot;	&quot;,<br> DATAFILE3[i],<br> &quot;	&quot;,<br> DATAFILE3[(i+1):min(i+6,length(DATAFILE3)+1)],<br> &quot;
&quot;)<br> }<br><br>Thanks for your time!<br><br>Sandra
